# TELE email-only runtime credentials: EXAMPLE, safe to keep in Git.
# For full INSTALL.sh setup (Dropbox, Tailscale, VNC etc.), use the repository's
# credentials.example.txt instead. This file is only for the installed mailer.
#
# Copy to /etc/tele/credentials.txt, root:root, mode 0600.
# Never replace placeholders with real secrets in THIS tracked example.
# Literal KEY=value; no quotes, shell expansion or inline password comments.
#
# Sender: the Google account that owns the app password below.
EMAIL_FROM=REPLACE_WITH_SENDER@gmail.com
# Recipient: the person who receives the station's status reports.
EMAIL_TO=REPLACE_WITH_REPORT_RECIPIENT@example.com
#
# Use a GOOGLE APP PASSWORD, not your normal Gmail/Google account password,
# not a six-digit verification code, and not a Dropbox or Tailscale credential.
# Enable 2-Step Verification for EMAIL_FROM, open Google Account > App passwords,
# and create an app password named for the station, for example "TELE station01".
# Paste its 16 characters WITHOUT any display spaces.
# Fake format demonstration: "abcd efgh ijkl mnop" becomes "abcdefghijklmnop".
# Neither demonstration is a working credential or a suggested password.
EMAIL_PASSWORD=REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_16_CHARACTER_GOOGLE_APP_PASSWORD
#
# Changing the main Google account password revokes its app passwords:
# create a replacement and update this station's private runtime file.
# If App passwords is unavailable, check account policy/Advanced Protection.
# Instructions: https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/185833?hl=en
